WEBVTT

00:03.000 --> 00:06.812
Every snippet comes from a storyboard entry like this.

00:06.900 --> 00:09.303
Display is what you see. It may be

00:09.403 --> 00:12.248
simplified, so the gate never checks it.

00:12.333 --> 00:15.953
Evidence is what the gate checks, in the cited lines.

00:19.050 --> 00:21.758
The gate reads those lines from disk.

00:21.850 --> 00:24.902
A plain token must match whole words, so

00:25.002 --> 00:27.582
a two is not found in twenty-four.

00:30.666 --> 00:34.070
Evidence must also reach both ends of the range.

00:34.166 --> 00:36.491
If code moves down a line, the

00:36.591 --> 00:40.210
range's first line usually loses its evidence.

00:40.300 --> 00:43.704
Then the cite fails instead of keeping its badge.

00:46.800 --> 00:51.212
A storyboard can also pin a commit for the badge to name.

00:51.300 --> 00:53.648
Then HEAD must match that commit.

00:53.733 --> 00:57.113
And uncommitted changes fail, unless allowed.

01:00.200 --> 01:02.692
All of this runs before rendering.

01:02.783 --> 01:07.267
One failure stops the render before any scene code exists.

01:07.366 --> 01:10.615
So a badge vouches for the cited evidence when

01:10.715 --> 01:13.818
the video was made, not for the explanation.
